# The screen reader (fm1-reader, announce.c), AMB-1's way: a reader listens, and each page, knob value, help card and
# button is said once, in the screen's own words (words.tsv says the short ones in full). A page is said when it
# settles: its name (a voice's page: the voice's too, as its title shows) and its four values; WHERE (or a reader
# that has just started) the whole screen: the page, the header, then what the page shows.
proj template full 0x5EED1234
wait 200
listen
wait 100
said HOME QUICK page: K1 Track PLUCK 1, K2 Generator SEED PROCEDURE, K3 Root A, K4 Scale NATURAL MINOR. Full ensemble, A NATURAL MINOR, tempo 96, stopped
# (what the page shows follows: the lanes, the horizon, the convergence)
listen
where
said Pluck 1, channel 1, 16 steps, 4 plays left; Pluck 2, channel 2, 15 steps
where
said Horizon: Pluck 1 may mutate, about 4 bars
where
said Convergence 1680 bars, about 4200 seconds. Tension 2. Degree 1
# a page settles before it is said
tap ENV
wait 300
said ENV TIMING page, Pluck 1: K1 Rate N/A, K2 Gate N/A, K3 Loop length 16 STEPS, K4 Phase 0
# MIDI channel access moved to ENV ROUTING; repeated short press cycles the section.
tap ENV
wait 300
said ENV ROUTING page, Pluck 1: K1 MIDI channel 1, K2 Register G2 to G4, K3 Unused -, K4 Unused -
# a knob: its name and value, once it settles
spin K1 2
wait 300
said K1 MIDI channel 3
spin K1 -2
wait 300
said K1 MIDI channel 1
# ROUTING's unused K3 has no effect and produces no parameter announcement
spin K3 1
wait 300
unsaid Loop
tap FX
wait 300
said FX MIDI DELAY page: K1 Delay OFF, K2 Time 1/8D, K3 Feedback 75%, K4 Decay 70%
where
said Pluck 1 off, 1/8D, feedback 75%, decay 70%, Pluck 2 off, 1/8D, feedback 75%, decay 70%
where
said Bass off, 1/8D, feedback 75%, decay 70%, Pad off, 1/8D, feedback 75%, decay 70%, Lead off, 1/8D, feedback 75%, decay 70%
where
said Heartbeat off, 1/8D, feedback 75%, decay 70%, at 96 BPM
tap GLO
wait 300
said Setup page: Root A, Sync INT, EXT input USB + TRS, Lights ON
where
said Seed 0000 0000 5EED 1234
spin K4 1
wait 300
said Lights KEYS
spin K4 -1
wait 300
tap SEQ
wait 300
said SEQ MOTION page: K1 Groove N/A, K2 Loop length 16 STEPS, K3 Phase 0, K4 Direction N/A
tap ARP
wait 300
said ARP HARMONY page, Pluck 1: K1 Generator SEED PROCEDURE, K2 Root A, K3 Scale NATURAL MINOR, K4 Direction N/A
# ARP K1 selects the generator; restore it after checking the announcement.
spin K1 1
wait 300
said K1 Generator PULSING BASS
spin K1 -1
wait 300
said K1 Generator SEED PROCEDURE
tap LFO
wait 300
said CC page, Pluck 1: Target FILTER CC 74, Cycle 16 BARS, Depth 30%, Scene NONE
tap HOME
wait 300
said HOME QUICK page
# the panel's messages, said once: PLAY, a mute, a degree
tap PLAY
said PLAYING FULL ENSEMBLE
wait 300
unsaid STOPPED
tapkey 2
said BASS MUTED
tapkey 2
said BASS ON
tapkey w4
said DEGREE 1 NEXT BAR
# HOME + SELECT: tempo is announced as a TEMPO message on every page
press HOME
spin SELECT 2
release HOME
wait 300
said TEMPO 98
tap ENV
wait 300
press HOME
spin SELECT -1
release HOME
said TEMPO 97
tap HOME
wait 300
# a help card: its button, then its lines
press FX
wait 1100
said FX button. MIDI NOTE DELAY. K1 ON/OFF, K2 TIME. K3 FEEDBACK, K4 DECAY
release FX
wait 100
# WHERE while playing: the header says so (the tempo sounding: the new one from the next bar)
wait 2600
where
said HOME QUICK page: K1 Track BASS, K2 Generator BASS MELODY, K3 Root A, K4 Scale NATURAL MINOR. Full ensemble, A NATURAL MINOR, tempo 97, playing
tap PLAY
said STOPPED
wait 300
# Real UI actions above must not have produced warnings. speakdump below deliberately
# prints the complete vocabulary, including WARN SAVE FAILED; that is not a failed save.
expect warns 0
# everything the reader can be told, for the audit (fm1-reader tools/audit.mjs)
speakdump
expect warns 0
